              "to": "iris.martinez@outlook.com",
              "subject": "Cooking class last night — homemade pasta & Bolognese",
              "body": "Hi Iris,\n\nI wanted to share a quick update from the cooking class I took last night with Chef Maria. We learned to make fresh pasta from scratch (kneading, resting, and rolling the dough thin) and a rich Bolognese sauce to go with it. Chef Maria shared a few great tips for perfect pasta texture: use a mix of flours (00 or all-purpose with a bit of semolina), hydrate the dough just enough, knead until smooth and elastic, and let it rest before rolling and cutting (tagliatelle or pappardelle work great).\n\nFor the Bolognese, we built flavor with a slow-sweated soffritto, browned meat (a mix of beef and pork), deglazed with wine, then simmered gently with tomato, a little milk, and plenty of time to develop depth.\n\nIt turned out fantastic — I’d love to make it for you sometime or share the recipe if you want.\n\nBest,"
